                <pb facs="0837" n="725" sameAs="frus:frus1919Russia/pg725"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.00/5414c: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Vice Consul at
                        Viborg</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Imbrie</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-10-17T13:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">October 17,
                                1919—1 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>In case Petrograd falls it is desired that you proceed there as soon as you
                    safely can and cable the Department at the earliest practicable moment a report
                    upon general conditions especially the material needs of the population. It is
                    expected that a part at least of your report will be given to the press
                    here.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Adee</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
